text: "---\nmodule: \"03-SALES-CLOSING\"\npart: \"A\"\ntitle: \"Discovery Call System\"\nversion: \"2026.05\"\nstatus: \"Production-Ready\"\n---\n\n# 03A: Discovery Call System\n\n> **Core Principle:** The discovery call is not a sales pitch. It is a diagnostic interview. Your job is to understand their pain so deeply that they convince themselves they need you.\n>\n> *\"Hey, can we schedule a quick Zoom call to discuss everything in detail?\"* — Him Singh\n\n---\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. [Pre-Call Setup](#1-pre-call-setup)\n2. [Call Qualification Framework](#2-call-qualification-framework)\n3. [The 7-Question Discovery Script](#3-the-7-question-discovery-script)\n4. [Call Notes & Documentation](#4-call-notes--documentation)\n5. [Post-Call Actions](#5-post-call-actions)\n6. [AI Prompts](#6-ai-prompts)\n7. [Action Checklist](#7-action-checklist)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Pre-Call Setup\n\n### Booking Page Configuration\n\n**Tools:** Calendly, TidyCal, Acuity Scheduling\n\n**Calendly Settings:**\n| Setting | Recommendation | Why |\n|---------|---------------|-----|\n| **Duration** | 30 minutes | Long enough to diagnose, short enough to respect time |\n| **Buffer** | 15 min before, 15 min after | Prep and debrief time |\n| **Availability** | Your working hours in client's timezone | Reduces friction |\n| **Questions** | 3 pre-call questions | Qualifies before the call |\n| **Reminder** | 24-hour + 1-hour email + SMS | Reduces no-shows |\n| **Brand** | Your logo, colors, custom URL | Professional impression |\n\n**Pre-Call Questions (Calendly Custom Fields):**\n```\n1. What specific challenge are you looking to solve? (required)\n2. What's your ideal timeline for this project? (required)\n3. Have you worked with a freelancer/agency before on similar work? (optional)\n```\n\n### Pre-Call Research Checklist\n\nBefore every call, spend 10 minutes researching:\n\n- [ ] Company website (products, team, recent news)\n- [ ] LinkedIn company page (hiring, posts, growth)\n- [ ] Crunchbase (funding, investors, competitors)\n- [ ] Their current tech stack (BuiltWith, Wappalyzer)\n- [ ] Recent press releases or blog posts\n- [ ] Competitor landscape (2-3 key competitors)\n\n### Pre-Call Mindset\n\n| Don't | Do |\n|-------|-----|\n| Pitch your services | Diagnose their pain |\n| Talk 80% of the time | Listen 80% of the time |\n| Quote prices early | Understand value first |\n| Promise everything | Set realistic expectations |\n| Rush to close | Build trust slowly |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Call Qualification Framework\n\n### BANT+ for Freelancers\n\n| Criteria | Question to Ask | Red Flag |\n|----------|----------------|----------|\n| **Budget** | \"What budget range have you allocated for this?\" | \"We don't have a budget yet\" |\n| **Authority** | \"Who else needs to approve this decision?\" | \"I need to check with my boss\" (no access to decision-maker) |\n| **Need** | \"What happens if this problem isn't solved in 6 months?\" | \"It's not really urgent\" |\n| **Timeline** | \"When do you need this delivered?\" | \"No specific deadline\" |\n| **+ Fit** | \"What does success look like for you?\" | Vague, unmeasurable goals |\n| **+ Pain** | \"How is this problem affecting revenue/operations today?\" | Can't quantify the pain |\n\n### The 3-Minute Opening\n\n**Minute 1: Rapport**\n```\n\"Thanks for making time, [Name]. Before we dive in, I did some homework \non [Company] — [specific observation from research]. That's impressive \ngrowth. How long have you been with the team?\"\n```\n\n**Minute 2: Agenda Setting**\n```\n\"Here's how I'd love to use our 30 minutes:\n1. First, understand your current situation and what's not working\n2. Then, explore what 'great' would look like for you\n3. Finally, if it makes sense, I'll share how I approach similar challenges\n\nDoes that work for you? Anything you want to make sure we cover?\"\n```\n\n**Minute 3: Permission to Ask Hard Questions**\n```\n\"I'm going to ask some direct questions about [pain area] — not to \nembarrass anyone, but to make sure I understand the real scope. \nIs that okay?\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. The 7-Question Discovery Script\n\n### Question 1: The Current State\n```\n\"Walk me through how you [handle this process] today. \nWhat does that look like from start to finish?\"\n```\n\n**What you're listening for:**\n- Manual steps that could be automated\n- Tools they're using (or not using)\n- Who else is involved in the process\n- Where things break down\n\n### Question 2: The Pain Point\n```\n\"Where does that process break down or cause the most friction? \nWhat takes the most time or creates the most headaches?\"\n```\n\n**What you're listening for:**\n- Specific pain (not vague complaints)\n- Frequency of the pain (daily? weekly?)\n- Who feels the pain (them? team? customers?)\n- Cost of the pain (time, money, opportunity)\n\n### Question 3: The Impact\n```\n\"If you had to put a number on it, how much is this costing you \nper month? In time, money, or missed opportunity?\"\n```\n\n**What you're listening for:**\n- Can they quantify the pain?\n- Is the number big enough to justify your fee?\n- Do they realize the full cost?\n\n### Question 4: The Attempted Solutions\n```\n\"What have you already tried to solve this? What worked and what didn't?\"\n```\n\n**What you're listening for:**\n- Previous freelancer/agency experience\n- In-house attempts (and why they failed)\n- Budget already spent on failed solutions\n- What they're NOT willing to try again\n\n### Question 5: The Ideal Outcome\n```\n\"If we were to check back in 90 days and this project was a massive \nsuccess, what would have changed? What metrics would be different?\"\n```\n\n**What you're listening for:**\n- Measurable success criteria\n- Realistic expectations\n- Timeline for results\n- Who defines \"success\"\n\n### Question 6: The Decision Process\n```\n\"Assuming we decide there's a good fit today, what would the next \nsteps look like on your end? Who else needs to be involved?\"\n```\n\n**What you're listening for:**\n- Decision-making process\n- Number of stakeholders\n- Approval timeline\n- Potential blockers\n\n### Question 7: The Investment Mindset\n```\n\"Projects like this typically require an investment of [range]. \nIs that in line with what you were expecting?\"\n```\n\n**What you're listening for:**\n- Budget reality check\n- Price sensitivity\n- Room for negotiation\n- Decision urgency\n\n---\n\n## 4. Call Notes & Documentation\n\n### The Discovery Call Notes Template\n\n```markdown\n# Discovery Call Notes: [Client Name] — [Date]\n\n## Basic Info\n- **Company:** [Name]\n- **Contact:** [Name, Title]\n- **Call Date:** [Date]\n- **Duration:** [Minutes]\n- **Source:** [How they found you]\n\n## Current State\n- **Process:** [How they do it today]\n- **Tools:** [What they use]\n- **Team:** [Who's involved]\n\n## Pain Points\n1. [Pain 1] — [Frequency] — [Cost]\n2. [Pain 2] — [Frequency] — [Cost]\n3. [Pain 3] — [Frequency] — [Cost]\n\n## Impact Quantification\n- **Time cost:** [Hours/month]\n- **Money cost:** [$/month]\n- **Opportunity cost:** [What's missed]\n- **Total estimated cost:** [$X/month or $Y/year]\n\n## Attempted Solutions\n- [Solution 1] — [Result]\n- [Solution 2] — [Result]\n\n## Ideal Outcome (90-Day Success)\n- **Metric 1:** [Target]\n- **Metric 2:** [Target]\n- **Metric 3:** [Target]\n\n## Decision Process\n- **Decision maker:** [Name/Title]\n- **Other stakeholders:** [Names]\n- **Approval timeline:** [Weeks]\n- **Budget range:** [$X - $Y]\n- **Expected start date:** [Date]\n\n## My Assessment\n- **Fit score:** [1-10]\n- **Red flags:** [Any concerns]\n- **Recommended approach:** [Starter/Pro/Enterprise]\n- **Estimated value:** [10-20% of their quantified pain]\n- **Proposed price:** [$Z]\n\n## Next Steps\n- [ ] Send proposal by [date]\n- [ ] Include: [specific items]\n- [ ] Follow up on: [date]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Post-Call Actions\n\n### The 24-Hour Rule\n\nWithin 24 hours of every discovery call:\n\n| Action | Time | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|\n| **Send thank-you email** | 2 hours | Gratitude + recap |\n| **Send proposal** | 24 hours | Strike while interest is hot |\n| **Calendar follow-up** | Immediate | Don't let it slip |\n\n### Thank-You Email Template\n\n```\nSubject: Great chatting, [Name] — here's what I heard\n\nHi [Name],\n\nThanks for making time today. I enjoyed learning about [Company]'s \nchallenges around [specific pain point].\n\nTo recap what I heard:\n• [Pain point 1] is costing you approximately [quantified cost]\n• [Pain point 2] is creating friction for [team/customers]\n• Your ideal 90-day outcome is [specific metric]\n\nBased on our conversation, I believe the [Starter/Pro/Enterprise] \napproach would be the best fit. I'm putting together a detailed \nproposal with scope, timeline, and investment — you'll have it \nby [day + time].\n\nIn the meantime, if any questions come up, just reply to this email \nor DM me on LinkedIn.\n\nLooking forward to potentially working together.\n\nBest,\n[Your name]\n[Portfolio link]\n[Calendly link]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. AI Prompts\n\n### Prompt 1: Discovery Call Prep\n\n```\nAct as a sales coach for freelance developers.\n\nI have a discovery call with:\n- Company: [COMPANY]\n- Contact: [NAME, TITLE]\n- Industry: [INDUSTRY]\n- Known pain: [PAIN POINT]\n\nCreate:\n1. 5 custom discovery questions based on their industry\n2. 3 potential objections they might raise\n3. 2 relevant case studies to reference\n4. 1 pricing anchor to test (value-based, not hourly)\n5. A 30-minute agenda (minute-by-minute)\n\nMake it specific to their situation. No generic advice.\n```\n\n### Prompt 2: Call Notes Analyzer\n\n```\nAct as a sales analyst.\n\nHere are my raw discovery call notes:\n[PASTE NOTES]\n\nAnalyze and provide:\n1. Fit score (1-10) with reasoning\n2. Recommended service tier (Starter/Pro/Enterprise)\n3. Suggested pricing (value-based calculation)\n4. Red flags or concerns\n5. Specific proposal angle\n6. Follow-up email draft\n\nBe direct and honest. If it's a bad fit, say so.\n```\n\n### Prompt 3: Objection Predictor\n\n```\nAct as a sales psychologist.\n\nBased on this discovery call context:\n- Client type: [TYPE]\n- Budget mentioned: [RANGE]\n- Previous experience: [GOOD/BAD/NONE]\n- Decision makers: [NUMBER]\n- Timeline: [URGENT/FLEXIBLE]\n\nPredict the top 5 objections they'll raise when seeing the proposal.\nFor each, provide:\n1. The objection (exact words they might use)\n2. Why they're really saying it (underlying fear)\n3. Your response (under 50 words)\n4. A question to redirect them\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Action Checklist\n\n### Before Your First Call\n\n- [ ] Set up Calendly/TidyCal with custom branding\n- [ ] Write 3 pre-call questions\n- [ ] Create call notes template (copy from above)\n- [ ] Practice the 7-question script with a friend\n- [ ] Set up recording (with permission) or note-taking system\n\n### After Every Call\n\n- [ ] Fill out call notes template within 30 minutes\n- [ ] Send thank-you email within 2 hours\n- [ ] Calculate value-based pricing (10-20% of quantified pain)\n- [ ] Draft proposal within 24 hours\n- [ ] Calendar follow-up for 3 days later\n- [ ] Update CRM/spreadsheet with status\n\n### Weekly Review\n\n- [ ] Review all discovery calls from the week\n- [ ] Calculate conversion rate (calls → proposals → closes)\n- [ ] Identify patterns in successful calls\n- [ ] Refine questions based on what worked\n- [ ] Update call script with new insights\n\n---\n\n> **Next:** [03B: Pricing Strategy →](03B-PRICING-STRATEGY.md)\n>\n> *\"The discovery call is where you earn the right to quote a price.\"*\n\n---\n\n*Module 03A | Discovery Call System | Version 2026.05*\n"
